  "result": "Fixed. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:34` was matching lines on the item's name instead of its SKU:\n\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.name != sku]   # before\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]    # after\n```\n\n`'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed. `Cart.add` already matches on `sku`, so `remove` now does the same.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, which is just the Gadget line. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- All 6 tests pass. pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest`, which the tests support.\n\nNone of the tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is why this bug got past them. I can add a regression test for it if you'd like.",
